   - The blocker runs BEGIN; UPDATE inventory SET qty = qty WHERE sku = 'SKU-HOT-1'; SELECT pg_sleep(3600); so it keeps the row lock for an hour, while the app's UPDATE inventory statements wait on Lock:tuple and Lock:transactionid.  [s4]
   - The database is not CPU or query-bound: the top statements are fast (sub-millisecond to ~50ms means), no deadlocks are reported, and total connections are 12 of 100.  [s5, s6, s4]
   - Payment_stub outbound p95 latency stayed around 0.1s during the incident, so the dependency is not the cause.  [s7]
  Fix: Terminate the stuck nightly_inventory_sync backend (pid 55047) to release the SKU-HOT-1 row lock, which unblocks the shop_api UPDATEs. Then fix the job: remove the pg_sleep/open transaction, and commit per batch or per SKU so no transaction is held across idle time. Optionally set idle_in_transaction_session_timeout and lock_timeout on the job role, and add a shop_api lock_timeout so requests fail fast instead of holding pool connections.

