   - Five shop_api UPDATE inventory sessions are blocked on Lock:tuple and Lock:transactionid, with the chain rooted at the sync session, and no deadlocks were recorded.  [s4, s5]
   - The blocked queries are simple indexed updates (mean about 0.04 ms for comparable queries), so the cause is lock wait and not a slow query. Postgres has 11 of 100 connections in use, so the connection limit is not the cause.  [s4, s6]
   - No deploys or config changes occurred in the last 3 hours, so the cause is the nightly job's open transaction and not a code release.  [s8]
  Fix: Kill the blocking backend pid 79230 (nightly_inventory_sync) to release SKU-HOT-1 and drain the shop_api pool. Then fix the sync job: it must not hold a transaction open across pg_sleep or other waits. Update the row in a short transaction, commit, and take locks in a consistent order. Add idle_in_transaction_session_timeout and lock_timeout on the DB role, and have the pool fail fast on checkout.

